 for the freestyle, actually losing a bit of ground to the Canadian, but winning by over 15 metres. Behind Gibson her teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/45873"} "Becky Smith"] " won the bronze medal, while Treiber trailed in fourth. David Wallechinsky, in " [:strong {} [:em {} "The Complete Book of the Olympics"]] ", notes Tauber was later revealed to have been given steroids from 1974 to 1980."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "114"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47547"} "Ulrike Tauber"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "4:51.24 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "4:42.77 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "45"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45793"} "Cheryl Gibson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "4:55.30 (2 h3)"] [:td {} "4:48.10 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "55"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45873"} "Becky Smith"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "4:52.90 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "4:50.48 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47550"} "Birgit Treiber"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:s